[MILESTONE 2] PYRAMID BLOCK (models/feudal_block.py) — COMPLETE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- SharedLatentProjection: RMSNorm(D) + Linear(D->L, no bias). One shared
  compressed coordinate system feeding BOTH overlords.
- Mamba2StateSpaceLayer (x2, alpha/beta, zero shared parameters): fused
  in_proj -> (z, x, B, C, dt); causal depthwise Conv1d over concat(x,B,C)
  with K-1 left padding; scalar-per-head A = -exp(A_log) (SSD form);
  dt = softplus(dt + dt_bias) with log-uniform init over [1e-3, 1e-1];
  pure-PyTorch sequential scan h_t = exp(dt*A) h_{t-1} + dt*(x_t (x) B_t),
  y_t = <h_t, C_t> + D_skip*x_t; gated RMSNorm output; out_proj(Di->L);
  residual. Recurrence is contractive by construction (A<0, dt>0).
- MinionExpert: SwiGLU FFN with gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj naming chosen to
  mirror Llama FFN modules so weight surgery is a pure tensor copy.
- MinionDispatchGate: float32 router softmax, top-k with renormalized combine
  weights, per-expert dispatch via index_add (clean autograd path — chosen
  over read-modify-write fancy indexing), Switch-style load-balance loss
  M * sum(f_e * pbar_e) surfaced in the aux dict.
- ConvergenceLayer: per-path RMSNorm + learned per-channel gates, concat to
  [B,S,2L], Cross-Level Structural Fusion Matrix W_fuse [2L->D] with
  1/sqrt(2L) init; block adds residual so it is near-identity at init.
- Every layer carries explicit shape comments ([B,S,D] -> [B,S,L] style).
- Config sanity (head divisibility, top-k bound, kernel >= 1) enforced in
  FeudalConfig.__post_init__ and covered by tests.

[MILESTONE 3] MAVERICK EXTENSION HOOKS (utils/weight_surgery.py) — COMPLETE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- CheckpointReader: uniform lazy tensor access over a single .safetensors
  file OR a sharded dir (via *.index.json weight_map, or shard enumeration
  when no index exists). Tensors read individually — the donor checkpoint
  never has to fit in memory.
- Dual layout auto-detection: fused HF Llama-4 (experts.gate_up_proj
  [n_exp, hidden, 2*ffn] + experts.down_proj) and per-expert
  (experts.{e}.gate_proj.weight etc.). Fused tensors are split and
  transposed to nn.Linear [out, in] convention.
- slice_to_geometry: leading-index truncation only; raises if the target dim
  exceeds the source dim (surgery never fabricates parameters).
- Round-robin cluster assignment: even source expert -> alpha slot e//2,
  odd -> beta slot e//2; 128 source experts fill 2x64 minion slots exactly.
- build_minion_fragment emits keys shaped like
  minions_alpha.experts.{m}.gate_proj.weight — loads straight into the block
  with load_state_dict(strict=False). CLI entry point included
  (python -m utils.weight_surgery CKPT --layer N --out fragment.pt).

